01:00:41,980 --> 01:00:43,330
大家都能以
And do the rest of you feel

884
01:00:43,350 --> 01:00:47,700
- “排除合理怀疑”作为评判依据吗？ - 是
- you can apply that idea, beyond a reasonable doubt, to this case? - Mhmm

885
01:00:47,720 --> 01:00:50,340
有多少人是父母？
How many of you have children?

886
01:00:50,610 --> 01:00:53,540
沃瓜德先生 有孩子？
Uh, Mr. Woguard. You have a child?

887
01:00:53,570 --> 01:00:56,350
嗯 是 索菲刚满四岁
Uh, yes. Soph just turned four.

888
01:00:56,370 --> 01:00:58,270
假设您女儿在公园
Say you and your daughter were at the park

889
01:00:58,290 --> 01:00:59,770
玩攀爬架
and she's playing on the monkey bars.

890
01:00:59,800 --> 01:01:01,690
您有几分钟没看她
And you turned your back for a few minutes,

891
01:01:01,720 --> 01:01:04,650
她跑过来说胳膊伤了
and then she runs over to you with a broken arm.

892
01:01:04,670 --> 01:01:06,060
您怎么判断？
What would you think happened?

893
01:01:06,080 --> 01:01:08,360
她从攀爬架上掉下来摔的
She fell off the monkey bars and broke her arm.

894
01:01:08,380 --> 01:01:11,740
对 这就是间接证据的例子
Yes, so that's an example of circumstantial evidence.

895
01:01:11,760 --> 01:01:15,560
根据事实可以做出的合理推断
That's what you can reasonably infer based on the facts that you have.

896
01:01:15,580 --> 01:01:17,630
沃瓜德先生 能明白吗
Does this make sense, Mr. Woguard?

897
01:01:17,650 --> 01:01:18,770
明白
Yes.

898
01:01:18,890 --> 01:01:21,480
要是有其他孩子跑来告诉您
And if instead another child ran over to you

899
01:01:21,510 --> 01:01:24,900
说看见她怎么摔的
and told you he saw her fall off the monkey bars,

900
01:01:24,940 --> 01:01:28,840
有人目击 这就是直接证词
that's direct testimony because someone witnessed it.

901
01:01:28,860 --> 01:01:31,260
大家能明白
Does everybody understand that difference,

902
01:01:31,280 --> 01:01:34,850
间接证据和直接证词的区别吗？
between circumstantial evidence and direct testimony?

903
01:01:34,880 --> 01:01:36,220
能
Mhmm.

904
01:01:36,240 --> 01:01:37,680
没有直接证词
Without direct testimony,

905
01:01:37,700 --> 01:01:41,570
就不能肯定犯罪一定发生
we cannot be positively certain a crime has been committed.

906
01:01:41,600 --> 01:01:43,020
作为检方
As the prosecution,

907
01:01:43,040 --> 01:01:46,680
我得把罪证明到排除合理怀疑
I must prove the defendant's guilt beyond a reasonable doubt.

908
01:01:46,710 --> 01:01:50,030
即 从现有的证据中
Meaning, that there is no other reasonable explanation

909
01:01:50,050 --> 01:01:52,440
不存在其他合理解释
that can come from evidence presented.

910
01:01:52,470 --> 01:01:54,990
谁是犯罪受害者
If any of you have been victims of a crime,

911
01:01:55,020 --> 01:01:56,870
请举手
please raise your hand.

912
01:01:57,680 --> 01:02:00,420
费伯先生 您遭遇了什么？
Uh, Mr. Faber, what was the crime?

913
01:02:00,450 --> 01:02:02,540
我被抢劫了 持枪的
Uh, I was robbed. At gunpoint.

914
01:02:02,560 --> 01:02:03,210
您认为
Do you have any reason to believe

915
01:02:03,240 --> 01:02:05,720
那次遭遇会妨碍您
that experience would make you unable to serve

916
01:02:05,750 --> 01:02:08,240
担任此庭公正陪审员吗？
as an impartial juror on this trial?

917
01:02:08,270 --> 01:02:09,440
不会
No.

918
01:02:11,040 --> 01:02:12,480
沃德小姐
Miss Ward.

919
01:02:13,630 --> 01:02:14,460
什么？
What?

920
01:02:14,490 --> 01:02:16,510
刚问到受害者时
When I asked who has been a victim of a crime,

921
01:02:16,540 --> 01:02:17,800
您举手了吧？
did you raise your hand?

922
01:02:17,820 --> 01:02:21,810
不是的 我不能讲这件事 就...
No, I realized I shouldn't share it. So...

923
01:02:21,830 --> 01:02:25,020
不能讲受害经历？
You're unable to share the crime?

924
01:02:27,200 --> 01:02:30,720
这样说吧 大庭广众说出来那事儿
It is frankly my worst nightmare to have to tell this whole room of strangers

925
01:02:30,750 --> 01:02:32,660
是我最害怕的
about the thing that happened to me.

926
01:02:32,690 --> 01:02:33,890
所以...
So...

927
01:02:33,920 --> 01:02:37,470
所以我才把手
that is the reasoning as to why I did not decide

928
01:02:37,500 --> 01:02:39,780
又放下来了
to continue having my hand raised.

929
01:02:39,800 --> 01:02:40,980
见谅
Thank you.

930
01:02:42,660 --> 01:02:45,660
那次遭遇会妨碍您
Do you think the crime would make you unable to serve

931
01:02:45,680 --> 01:02:48,170
担任此庭公正陪审员吗？
as an impartial juror on this case?

932
